<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alzey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alzey is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, in the hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a> south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>. It grew around a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Staufer</a> castle and from the 13th century was a centre of power of the counts palatine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, with a castle and administrative district. It is the main town of a wine-growing area and appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nibelungenlied">Nibelungenlied</a> as the home of the minstrel Volker.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alzey.jpg" alt="Alzey" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flodur63 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alzey_-_Altstadt_m_Stiftskirche_v_O.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
